ent code to see how it handles compact size.\n\nLooking at the Menu.tsx code:\n```javascript\nconst MenuItem = forwardRef<HTMLDivElement, MenuItemProps>(\n  (\n    {\n      label,\n      icon,\n      shortcut,\n      danger = false,\n      size = 'default',\n      onSelect,\n      className,\n      disabled,\n      ...props\n    },\n    ref,\n  ) => {\n```\n\nI see that MenuItem has a `size` prop with default 'default'. The issue is that the current HomePage.tsx doesn't specify `size=\"compact\"` for the MenuItem. Let me check if this is needed by looking at the design again.\n\nActually, wait. The design shows that the Sign Out Item in the User Menu is using the Menu Item component (ZsXwz), which is the \"compact\" size. But looking at the HomePage.tsx, I see it's just using `<MenuItem ... />` without specifying size.\n\nLet me check what the default size is and whether I need to change it. Looking at the Menu.tsx:\n```javascript\nsize = 'default',\n```\n\nSo the default size is 'default', not 'compact'. Since the design shows the Menu Item component (ZsXwz) with compact sizing, I should update the HomePage to use `size=\"compact\"`.\n\nHowever, before I make this change, let me think about whether this is actually necessary. The issue says \"Build to the claimed parts' JSON; this issue does not repeat their values.\" This means I should match the design exactly.\n\nBut wait - looking at the test that's already passing:\n```\nGiven I am signed in as Mara Reyes, when I open the user card's menu, then I see \"Mara Reyes\", my email and \"Sign out\"\n```\n\nThis test already passes, which means the current implementation is showing the right content. However, the styling might not be exactly matching the design.\n\nLet me verify if there are any visual differences by checking the component more carefully. Looking at the Menu Item design (ZsXwz.json):\n- padding: [7, 9] means padding-top/bottom: 7, padding-left/right: 9\n- gap: 9\n- cornerRadius: 6\n- Icon width/height